ver again is an  incredibly important thing i think those  programs could be expanded without going  too much into taxpayer pockets and i  believe that everybody should have  access to those programs right now the  da's office is kind of gatekeeping  everyone should be able to apply it  shouldn't be which prosecutor you get  decides what program you can go into  you can watch more of our interview with  mr treffinger including what he thinks  about the death penalty at eight newsnow  dot com  are we in a recession or not next on  politics now steps the federal  government is taking to slow down  inflation and the debate over what  actually counts as a recession plus  holding rental companies accountable  congress calls out one of nevada's  biggest for its treatment of tenants  politics now  toyota let's go places  welcome back to politics now  nevada democrats are still waiting to  see if the silver state gets to pick a  presidential candidate first in 2024 at  their last meeting the democratic  national committee floated the idea of  having nevada and new hampshire's  primary on the same day the  congressional hispanic caucus and the  latino victory fund have both endorsed  nevada going first in the primary  schedule a first vote a vote rather a  first vote on who would go first that is  scheduled to take place the first week  of august which is next week a final  decision is expected in the next month  or so  all right congress is considering a bill  which allows medicare to set drug prices  nevada senator catherine cortez masto  says ads being run against the  legislation and against her are  misleading this ad  incorrectly claims that i support a bill  that would strip  300 billion dollars from medicare  this couldn't be further from the truth  what i do know is that  the ad is a deliberate lie  so this ad the senator is talking about  is from a dark money group called  american prosperity alliance  it refers to a portion of president joe  biden's buildback better plan which  deals with prescription drugs it would  let medicare directly negotiate  prescription prices with drug companies  the congressional budget office  estimates it would save 288 billion  dollars over 10 years senator cortez  masto's office says that money will be  used to cut out of pocket costs on  medicare part d and continue affordable  care act tax credits  this week the federal reserve announced  it will raise interest rates for the  fourth time this year  the move is designed to help curb  inflation and fight off a potential  recession washington d.c correspondent  rashad hudson reports  interest rates are headed up again for  the fourth time since march the federal  reserve is raising interest rates this  time by three quarters of a point these  rate hikes have been large and they've  come  they've come quickly and  it's likely that their full effect has  not been felt by the economy this will  impact people buying cars houses or  taking out a loan fed chair jerome  powell says the increase is necessary to  slow the economy and reduce the 9.1  percent inflation rate the highest in  nearly 40 years we didn't expect a good  reading but this one  this one was was even worse than  expected i would say powell aims for  inflation to be around two percent while  the white house argues that the u.s is  not headed for a recession senate  republican leader mitch mcconnell  doesn't believe it clearly something  isn't adding up house republicans like  louisiana congressman steve scalise say  president biden's policies are driving  up inflation joe biden won't look the  american people in the eye and admit  that his programs have failed chairman  powell says there will likely be another  rate hike in september how much depends  on what's up with inflation we need to  see inflation coming down  that was rashad hudson reporting it was  the second straight quarter of negative  gdp growth as well that has been a  marker of a recession in the past  a clark county l